THIRD-PARTY CODE AND WEIGHTS VENDORED INTO THIS CRATE: NONE.

No source file, model file, or weight tensor in this directory is derived from a third-party
watermarking implementation. The architecture this crate hosts is specified in
docs/WATERMARK_N_SPEC.md and is a clean-room design written from published paper text.

Deliberately not vendored, with the licence position read from the primary artifact:

  SilentCipher (Sony)   github.com/sony/silentcipher
                        Code MIT. The release tarball contains no LICENSE, NOTICE or COPYING, and
                        the repository README scopes its grant to "the code in this repository".
                        The HuggingFace mirror has cardData: null and no licence file. THE WEIGHTS
                        CARRY NO GRANT and are not used.

  DeepAWR               Declares MIT, but 26% / 43% / 39% of substantive lines in train_audio.py,
                        extract.py and embed.py are verbatim from DeAR, an unlicensed drop, with
                        disjoint author sets. An MIT grant cannot convey rights the grantor does
                        not hold. Reference document only: never a dependency, never vendored.

  DeAR                  Unlicensed Google Drive distribution. Not vendorable. Its published
                        analytic distortion-layer recipe is a fact in a paper and is used as such
                        by the training harness; no code or weights are taken.

  AudioSeal (Meta)      github.com/facebookresearch/audioseal - MIT on code and, since 2024-04-02,
                        on weights; training code released 2024-06-17; MIT ONNX export at
                        synath/audioseal-onnx. The only fully licence-clean pipeline in the field.
                        The training harness forks it. THIS CRATE VENDORS NEITHER ITS CODE NOR ITS
                        WEIGHTS: the inference path here is written against ONNX Runtime directly.

RUNTIME DEPENDENCY:

  ort                   crates.io/crates/ort 2.0.0-rc.13 - MIT OR Apache-2.0. A Rust binding to
                        ONNX Runtime; linked, not vendored.
  ONNX Runtime          github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime - MIT. Obtained at build time by the
                        `download-binaries` feature, or supplied by the host through
                        `load-dynamic`. Not redistributed by this crate.

FIXTURE MODELS:

  fixtures/*.onnx are emitted by tools/make_fixture_models.py in this directory. They are
  hand-written arithmetic graphs with no learned parameters and no third-party provenance.
